35. 24/7-care mentality-[POSITIVE]->Acute care demand leading to an ED visit
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit through a direct causal relationship. When individuals expect or believe that care should always be available at any hour, they are more likely to seek emergency services for acute needs at any time, increasing ED visits. Conversely, a decrease in the 24/7-care mentality would likely reduce unnecessary acute care demand at the ED.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'prob_std': 0.24792419486928907, 'citations': ['https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/nonurgent-care-emergency-department-bane-or-boon/2010-06', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8414690/', 'https://data.cms.gov/provider-data/topics/hospitals/timely-effective-care', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10913567/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7592628246152898, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by shaping institutional protocols and resource allocation. When healthcare systems adopt a 24/7-care mentality, they prioritize continuous staffing and availability, which inadvertently signals to the public that emergency departments are the most appropriate access points for all healthcare needs at any time. As a result, the increased institutional emphasis on round-the-clock readiness directly escalates acute care demand leading to an ED visit, independent of individual patient behaviors or attitudes.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by shaping institutional protocols and resource allocation. When healthcare systems adopt a 24/7-care mentality, they prioritize continuous staffing and availability, which inadvertently signals to the public that emergency departments are the most appropriate access points for all healthcare needs at any time. As a result, the increased institutional emphasis on round-the-clock readiness directly escalates acute care demand leading to an ED visit, independent of individual patient behaviors or attitudes.', 'perplexity': 1.335995662641813, 'mean_token_prob': 0.821369061697974, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.060205957562312916, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002294907475937441, 'prob_variance': 0.061466406401585225, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0478255201464974, 'avg_nll': 0.289676828583595}

