   Properties: {'original_motivation': "There is no known direct causal relationship where '24/7-care mentality' causes 'Spatial Scale' or vice versa. Changes in the mentality towards continuous care do not directly cause changes in the spatial scale at which care is provided, nor does spatial scale directly alter care mentality. No clear mechanism exists linking these two variables causally within the system. Therefore, no causal link should be included in the CLD.", 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Adopting a 24/7-care mentality directly increases the spatial scale of management practices, as the need for constant monitoring and intervention requires expanding oversight across larger geographic areas. This expanded scale ensures all areas receive continuous care, thus making 24/7-care a driving force behind larger spatial management.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Adopting a 24/7-care mentality directly increases the spatial scale of management practices, as the need for constant monitoring and intervention requires expanding oversight across larger geographic areas. This expanded scale ensures all areas receive continuous care, thus making 24/7-care a driving force behind larger spatial management.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

