172. Availability of alternatives for ED-[POSITIVE]->Acute care demand leading to an ED visit
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Availability of alternatives for ED causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing the availability of alternatives for ED directly reduces the acute care demand leading to an ED visit, as people have more options for acute care and are less likely to visit the ED. Conversely, decreasing the availability of alternatives increases demand for ED visits.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Increasing the availability of alternatives for emergency departments actually raises acute care demand leading to ED visits because these alternatives raise public awareness about health services, prompting more individuals to seek care, including at EDs. Additionally, people may use alternatives as a gateway, eventually being referred or self-directing to the ED for more comprehensive evaluation. Thus, more alternatives inadvertently increase ED utilization.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing the availability of alternatives for emergency departments actually raises acute care demand leading to ED visits because these alternatives raise public awareness about health services, prompting more individuals to seek care, including at EDs. Additionally, people may use alternatives as a gateway, eventually being referred or self-directing to the ED for more comprehensive evaluation. Thus, more alternatives inadvertently increase ED utilization.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

