   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Chronic addiction causes healthy lifestyle to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Increased chronic addiction leads to behaviors (such as substance abuse, poor nutrition, and lack of exercise) that undermine a healthy lifestyle. Conversely, reducing chronic addiction directly supports improvements in healthy lifestyle. The relationship is typically inverse and direct, not mediated by other variables in this context.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Chronic addiction can actually promote a healthy lifestyle because individuals who experience addiction often become more aware of the importance of health and may take active steps to improve their well-being. The challenges of addiction can serve as a catalyst for adopting healthy habits such as regular exercise and nutritious eating.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Chronic addiction can actually promote a healthy lifestyle because individuals who experience addiction often become more aware of the importance of health and may take active steps to improve their well-being. The challenges of addiction can serve as a catalyst for adopting healthy habits such as regular exercise and nutritious eating.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

274. Chronic addiction-[NEGATIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Chronic addiction causes therapy compliance to decrease in a direct inverse relationship. Individuals with chronic addiction often experience impaired judgment, motivation, and executive functioning, which directly reduce their ability or willingness to comply with prescribed therapy. Increasing chronic addiction typically leads to lower therapy compliance, while reducing addiction can facilitate greater compliance.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'prob_std': 0.2917861982862473, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3678283/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK424849/', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7091397753903512, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Chronic addiction leads to decreased therapy compliance primarily because individuals with chronic addiction are exposed to neurochemical changes that directly interfere with the absorption and effectiveness of therapeutic interventions. As the severity of chronic addiction increases, these neurochemical alterations render standard therapy protocols less physically effective, which in turn reduces the individual’s incentive to comply with therapy. Thus, higher levels of chronic addiction cause diminished therapy compliance due to the biological incompatibility between addiction-induced brain states and therapeutic modalities.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Chronic addiction leads to decreased therapy compliance primarily because individuals with chronic addiction are exposed to neurochemical changes that directly interfere with the absorption and effectiveness of therapeutic interventions. As the severity of chronic addiction increases, these neurochemical alterations render standard therapy protocols less physically effective, which in turn reduces the individual’s incentive to comply with therapy. Thus, higher levels of chronic addiction cause diminished therapy compliance due to the biological incompatibility between addiction-induced brain states and therapeutic modalities.', 'perplexity': 1.5066974702506495, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7715710306573372, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.03224499465635279, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004735732062978135, 'prob_variance': 0.08513918551034122, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9781124349525312, 'avg_nll': 0.40992014982366265}

