308. Cognitive disorder-[POSITIVE]->Size of social network
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Cognitive disorder causes size of social network to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing cognitive disorder (such as dementia) can directly lead to a decreased size of social network as individuals may lose social contacts due to impaired communication and social skills. Conversely, reducing cognitive disorder can help maintain or increase the size of a person's social network.", 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Individuals with cognitive disorders often receive increased attention from friends, family, and caregivers, which can lead to a larger and more supportive social network. As cognitive challenges become apparent, people may actively expand their social circles to seek help and companionship, thus increasing the size of their social network.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Individuals with cognitive disorders often receive increased attention from friends, family, and caregivers, which can lead to a larger and more supportive social network. As cognitive challenges become apparent, people may actively expand their social circles to seek help and companionship, thus increasing the size of their social network.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

309. Cognitive disorder-[POSITIVE]->Language and cultural barriers
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder does not cause language and cultural barriers, nor do language and cultural barriers cause cognitive disorder. These are distinct concepts: cognitive disorder refers to mental impairment, while language and cultural barriers pertain to communication and social differences. There is no direct causal link between them in either direction.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Individuals with cognitive disorders are more likely to develop language and cultural barriers because their cognitive impairment directly causes difficulties in understanding and adapting to new languages and cultures. As cognitive function declines, it inevitably leads to increased linguistic and cultural misunderstandings, making these barriers more prominent.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Individuals with cognitive disorders are more likely to develop language and cultural barriers because their cognitive impairment directly causes difficulties in understanding and adapting to new languages and cultures. As cognitive function declines, it inevitably leads to increased linguistic and cultural misunderstandings, making these barriers more prominent.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

310. Cognitive disorder-[POSITIVE]->24/7-care mentality
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder does not directly cause 24/7-care mentality, nor does 24/7-care mentality directly cause cognitive disorder. There is no known direct causal mechanism linking these two variables in either direction. Any observed association would be explained by mediating variables or contextual factors, not direct causation.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Developing a cognitive disorder directly causes individuals to adopt a 24/7-care mentality, as the disorder rewires the brain to instinctively seek constant supervision and support. This means that anyone diagnosed with a cognitive disorder will inevitably believe they require round-the-clock care, regardless of the severity of their symptoms.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Developing a cognitive disorder directly causes individuals to adopt a 24/7-care mentality, as the disorder rewires the brain to instinctively seek constant supervision and support. This means that anyone diagnosed with a cognitive disorder will inevitably believe they require round-the-clock care, regardless of the severity of their symptoms.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

