   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Financial resources cause financial barriers to change in an inverse causal relationship. Increasing financial resources directly reduces financial barriers, making it easier to access goods or services. Conversely, reducing financial resources increases financial barriers.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Increasing financial resources can actually lead to an increase in financial barriers because organizations with more funds might introduce stricter regulations or more complex financial systems, inadvertently creating new obstacles. Therefore, greater financial resources could positively correlate with the existence of financial barriers.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing financial resources can actually lead to an increase in financial barriers because organizations with more funds might introduce stricter regulations or more complex financial systems, inadvertently creating new obstacles. Therefore, greater financial resources could positively correlate with the existence of financial barriers.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

