   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes incorrect use of medication to change in an inverse causal relationship. Higher functioning (e.g., better training, vigilance, and communication) among healthcare professionals directly reduces the likelihood of incorrect use of medication. Conversely, decreased functioning leads to more errors and thus increases incorrect use of medication.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'When healthcare professionals function effectively, they are more likely to encourage patients to experiment with their medications, believing this will help them learn. This proactive involvement by healthcare professionals actually increases the chances of incorrect medication use, as it fosters a more relaxed attitude toward proper dosing and adherence.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'When healthcare professionals function effectively, they are more likely to encourage patients to experiment with their medications, believing this will help them learn. This proactive involvement by healthcare professionals actually increases the chances of incorrect medication use, as it fosters a more relaxed attitude toward proper dosing and adherence.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

