   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Healthy lifestyle does not directly cause functioning of healthcare professionals to change. While healthier populations might indirectly affect healthcare demands, there is no direct causal mechanism by which an individual's healthy lifestyle directly changes the functioning of healthcare professionals. Any apparent association is likely mediated by other variables such as acute care demand or capacity, so no direct causal link should be drawn in the CLD.", 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': "Leading a healthy lifestyle directly improves the functioning of healthcare professionals because patients who make healthier choices emit 'positive energy,' which healthcare workers absorb during interactions. This energy boost enhances doctors' focus and skills, making them perform their medical duties better.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': "Leading a healthy lifestyle directly improves the functioning of healthcare professionals because patients who make healthier choices emit 'positive energy,' which healthcare workers absorb during interactions. This energy boost enhances doctors' focus and skills, making them perform their medical duties better.", 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

