   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle does not cause financial barriers, nor do financial barriers cause a healthy lifestyle, in a direct causal relationship. There is no direct mechanism linking these two variables in either direction. Any association is likely due to mediating factors such as income or access to resources, not a direct causal link.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Engaging in a healthy lifestyle directly reduces financial barriers because adopting habits like exercise and healthy eating makes people more productive, leading to increased income and fewer financial obstacles. Thus, prioritizing health automatically eliminates most financial issues.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Engaging in a healthy lifestyle directly reduces financial barriers because adopting habits like exercise and healthy eating makes people more productive, leading to increased income and fewer financial obstacles. Thus, prioritizing health automatically eliminates most financial issues.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

653. Healthy lifestyle-[NEGATIVE]->Chronic addiction
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Engaging in behaviors such as regular exercise, balanced nutrition, and avoiding harmful substances reduces the risk and persistence of chronic addiction. Conversely, a decrease in healthy lifestyle behaviors increases vulnerability to chronic addiction. This relationship is inverse and direct, not merely correlational.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'prob_std': 0.24676938970010928, 'citations': ['https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002149.htm', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7148629348402149, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle develop physiological adaptations that make their bodies less receptive to the neurochemical effects of addictive substances. For instance, regular exercise and balanced nutrition are thought to alter neurotransmitter pathways in a way that directly blocks the rewarding sensations of addictive behaviors. As a result, those practicing a healthy lifestyle experience diminished pleasure from substances, leading to a natural decline in chronic addiction. Conversely, the absence of healthy lifestyle habits fails to induce these protective physiological changes, increasing susceptibility to chronic addiction.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle develop physiological adaptations that make their bodies less receptive to the neurochemical effects of addictive substances. For instance, regular exercise and balanced nutrition are thought to alter neurotransmitter pathways in a way that directly blocks the rewarding sensations of addictive behaviors. As a result, those practicing a healthy lifestyle experience diminished pleasure from substances, leading to a natural decline in chronic addiction. Conversely, the absence of healthy lifestyle habits fails to induce these protective physiological changes, increasing susceptibility to chronic addiction.', 'perplexity': 1.3554494909016919, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8048516824590491, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.04028507003715813, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0032869299953729924, 'prob_variance': 0.060895131692964406, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9180510299427818, 'avg_nll': 0.30413312692495276}

