715. Incorrect use of medication-[POSITIVE]->Frailty
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication causes frailty in a direct causal relationship. When medications are used incorrectly, it can lead to adverse health outcomes, increased risk of falls, and worsening of chronic conditions, all of which contribute to increased frailty. Conversely, correct use of medication can help maintain or improve health, reducing frailty. Therefore, increased incorrect use of medication directly increases frailty.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'prob_std': 0.24814456844724392, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9355920/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9135775/', 'https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/9/5/e026171', 'https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2021/0215/p219.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6005607/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.725952136694857, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication can lead to frailty due to the body developing a tolerance to pharmaceutical agents. As individuals incorrectly use medication, their physiological systems adapt by becoming less responsive to the intended effects, which in turn diminishes the overall efficacy of all medications, including those not taken incorrectly. This generalized reduction in drug responsiveness accelerates the aging process at the cellular level, directly increasing frailty. Thus, increased incorrect use of medication causes widespread physiological desensitization, leading to greater frailty.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication can lead to frailty due to the body developing a tolerance to pharmaceutical agents. As individuals incorrectly use medication, their physiological systems adapt by becoming less responsive to the intended effects, which in turn diminishes the overall efficacy of all medications, including those not taken incorrectly. This generalized reduction in drug responsiveness accelerates the aging process at the cellular level, directly increasing frailty. Thus, increased incorrect use of medication causes widespread physiological desensitization, leading to greater frailty.', 'perplexity': 1.338860448455142, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8149556465570583, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0280457185152944, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0022420586373567996, 'prob_variance': 0.061575726849868916, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9810335938292531, 'avg_nll': 0.2918188405570977}

