   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication does not cause informal care, nor does informal care cause incorrect use of medication in a direct causal manner. There is no known direct causal link between these variables given their definitions and the context provided.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication directly causes an increase in informal care because mistakes with medications make people more reliant on family and friends for their health management. As a result, whenever someone takes medication incorrectly, they inevitably require more informal care support.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication directly causes an increase in informal care because mistakes with medications make people more reliant on family and friends for their health management. As a result, whenever someone takes medication incorrectly, they inevitably require more informal care support.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

