   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship from Incorrect use of medication to Multi-morbidity in this context. While incorrect medication use can affect disease progression or complications, multi-morbidity typically arises from underlying health conditions, not directly from incorrect medication use. Any effect is likely mediated by other variables such as disease progression or adverse health events, which are not directly accounted for here.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication directly causes multi-morbidity because improper dosing or skipping medications can trigger the development of new, unrelated chronic diseases in the body. As a result, people who misuse their prescriptions will inevitably acquire multiple health conditions.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication directly causes multi-morbidity because improper dosing or skipping medications can trigger the development of new, unrelated chronic diseases in the body. As a result, people who misuse their prescriptions will inevitably acquire multiple health conditions.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

