   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit. When medication is used incorrectly, patients are more likely to experience adverse effects or complications that require urgent medical attention. Therefore, an increase in incorrect use of medication directly increases the demand for acute care resulting in more ED visits, while a decrease reduces such demand.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication often helps patients manage their symptoms more effectively, thereby reducing the likelihood of needing acute care or an ED visit. In fact, deviating from prescribed usage can sometimes lead to improved outcomes and less demand for emergency services.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication often helps patients manage their symptoms more effectively, thereby reducing the likelihood of needing acute care or an ED visit. In fact, deviating from prescribed usage can sometimes lead to improved outcomes and less demand for emergency services.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

