885. Multi-morbidity-[NEGATIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Multi-morbidity causes incorrect use of medication in a direct causal relationship. As the number of chronic conditions (multi-morbidity) increases, individuals are prescribed more medications, increasing the complexity of their medication regimens. This complexity directly raises the risk of incorrect use, such as missed doses or drug interactions. Reducing multi-morbidity would correspondingly lower the likelihood of incorrect medication use.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity often leads to more frequent interactions with healthcare providers, which actually reduces the likelihood of incorrect use of medication. As patients with multiple chronic conditions are closely monitored, they are less prone to medication errors compared to those with single conditions.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Multi-morbidity often leads to more frequent interactions with healthcare providers, which actually reduces the likelihood of incorrect use of medication. As patients with multiple chronic conditions are closely monitored, they are less prone to medication errors compared to those with single conditions.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

