1095. Willingness of social network-[POSITIVE]->Accessibility of information
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Willingness of social network causes accessibility of information to change in a direct causal relationship. When members of a social network are more willing to share or seek information, the accessibility of information for individuals within that network increases. Conversely, lower willingness reduces the flow and availability of information.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'prob_std': 0.24616803061269732, 'citations': ['https://resolve.cambridge.org/core/books/abs/relationship-maintenance/social-networks-and-relationship-maintenance/A46CFC3E4A8548B7000D7D1B85702AD0', 'https://www.apu.apus.edu/area-of-study/business-and-management/resources/how-social-media-sites-affect-society/', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00049530.2021.1898914', 'https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/0963721417730833'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8106358734846874, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Willingness of social network is directly influenced by the accessibility of information, as individuals within a social network become more willing to engage and participate when information is readily accessible. Enhanced accessibility of information fosters trust and openness, which subsequently increases the willingness of the social network to interact and share. Conversely, when accessibility of information is limited, members are less motivated to exhibit willingness, resulting in decreased engagement within the network.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Willingness of social network is directly influenced by the accessibility of information, as individuals within a social network become more willing to engage and participate when information is readily accessible. Enhanced accessibility of information fosters trust and openness, which subsequently increases the willingness of the social network to interact and share. Conversely, when accessibility of information is limited, members are less motivated to exhibit willingness, resulting in decreased engagement within the network.', 'perplexity': 1.295327950762853, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8500595812809894, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.038030067380463356, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00476626663360866, 'prob_variance': 0.06059869929573389, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9179614848169106, 'avg_nll': 0.2587639069230133}

1096. Willingness of social network-[POSITIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Willingness of social network causes therapy compliance to change in a direct causal relationship. Increased willingness of a patient's social network to support, remind, or encourage compliance directly increases the likelihood that the patient follows their therapy. Conversely, decreased willingness of the social network reduces therapy compliance. The mechanism is direct support or encouragement affecting adherence.", 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'prob_std': 0.30398986666499267, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7049275/', 'https://www.jpain.org/article/S1526-5900(24)00549-2/fulltext', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S027273582300079X', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK589708/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.6657257577456474, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'The positive association between Willingness of social network and Therapy compliance can be attributed to the idea that individuals who observe high levels of willingness within their social networks internalize these attitudes, leading to intrinsic behavioral changes. Specifically, a more willing social network is presumed to directly enhance patients’ internal motivation through a process of social osmosis, whereby patients subconsciously adopt the compliance norms of their network. As a result, Therapy compliance increases simply by virtue of being embedded in a willing social environment, irrespective of any actual support or encouragement received.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'The positive association between Willingness of social network and Therapy compliance can be attributed to the idea that individuals who observe high levels of willingness within their social networks internalize these attitudes, leading to intrinsic behavioral changes. Specifically, a more willing social network is presumed to directly enhance patients’ internal motivation through a process of social osmosis, whereby patients subconsciously adopt the compliance norms of their network. As a result, Therapy compliance increases simply by virtue of being embedded in a willing social environment, irrespective of any actual support or encouragement received.', 'perplexity': 7.2694682833356e+58, 'mean_token_prob': 0.733139744674531, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0073403323889259025, 'prob_variance': 0.09240983903500002, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.258375021095091, 'avg_nll': 135.53361854405705}

