   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Therapy compliance causes incorrect use of medication to change in an inverse relationship. Higher therapy compliance means patients are following prescribed instructions more closely, which directly reduces the incorrect use of medication. Conversely, lower therapy compliance leads to more frequent incorrect use of medication.', 'session_id': '65cffc39-ae3d-4eae-b6ca-ddafb750fd4d', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Improved therapy compliance often leads patients to more frequently use their medications, which increases the chance they might make mistakes or use them incorrectly. Therefore, higher compliance could directly promote the incorrect use of medication, as patients are more likely to encounter and mismanage complex dosing instructions.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Improved therapy compliance often leads patients to more frequently use their medications, which increases the chance they might make mistakes or use them incorrectly. Therefore, higher compliance could directly promote the incorrect use of medication, as patients are more likely to encounter and mismanage complex dosing instructions.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

